      "title": "Dates Description Links",
      "path": "Current_Affairs/Important_Current_Affairs/Dates_Description_Links.txt",
      "format": "TXT",
      "bytes": 5522,
      "url": "https://github.com/madhurimarawat/UPSC-Notes-Resources/blob/3e9d46ce703ce18b9a161ca4b8819f789f31de46/Current_Affairs/Important_Current_Affairs/Dates_Description_Links.txt",
      "text": "1. Act East Policy — 13 November 2014\r\nThe Act East Policy was launched by Prime Minister Narendra Modi at the 9th East Asia Summit in Nay Pyi Taw, Myanmar, emphasising stronger ties with ASEAN and East Asian nations.\r\nSource: Jagran Josh\r\n🔗 https://www.jagranjosh.com/general-knowledge/act-east-policy-of-india-meaning-and-objectives-1527251668-1\r\n\r\n2. Bhashini (National Language Translation Mission) — August 2022\r\nThe Indian government launched Bhashini at Gandhinagar, Gujarat, under the National Language Translation Mission to enable multilingual access to digital content.\r\nSource: Wikipedia\r\n🔗 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhashini\r\n\r\n3. US Tariffs on Indian Goods (“Liberation Day” Tariffs) — 2 April 2025\r\nOn 2 April 2025, the United States announced reciprocal tariffs on Indian imports, often referred to as “Liberation Day” tariffs, imposing about a 26% tariff rate on Indian goods in a protectionist trade move.\r\nSource: The Indian Express\r\n🔗 https://indianexpress.com/article/india/donald-trump-liberation-day-reciprocal-tariffs-india-26-percent-9921154/\r\n\r\n4. Operation Sindoor — 7 May 2025 (approx.)\r\n“Operation Sindoor” was reported as coordinated strikes on terror infrastructure sites carried out on 7 May 2025.\r\nSource: Scribd (reported document)\r\n🔗 https://www.scribd.com/document/operation-sindoor-report\r\n\r\n5. Ahmedabad Plane Tragedy — 12 June 2025\r\nOn 12 June 2025, Air India Flight AI171, a Boeing 787-8 Dreamliner, crashed shortly after takeoff from Ahmedabad bound for London Gatwick, killing hundreds and injuring others.\r\nSource: Wikipedia (Air India Flight 171 crash)\r\n🔗 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_India_Flight_171\r\n\r\n6. NCP 25 (National Cooperation Policy 2025, India) — 24 July 2025\r\nThe National Cooperation Policy 2025 was launched on 24 July 2025 to strengthen cooperative institutions and enhance intergovernmental collaboration in India.\r\nSource: YouTube official video release (government channel)\r\n🔗 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=njU3A2uXeG8\r\n\r\n7. Chess World Cup 2025 — 28 July 2025\r\nOn 28 July 2025, IM Divya Deshmukh became the fourth Indian woman to earn the Grandmaster title during the Chess World Cup 2025.\r\nSource: Chess.com\r\n🔗 https://www.chess.com/news/view/divya-deshmukh-india-grandmaster\r\n\r\n8. UNESCO Tentative Sites (India: 7 New Natural Sites) — 12 September 2025\r\nOn 12 September 2025, India added seven natural heritage sites to its UNESCO Tentative List, expanding its candidature for future inscription.\r\nSource: Sahapedia (official statement)\r\n🔗 https://www.sahapedia.org/india-unesco-tentative-list-2025\r\n\r\n9. Viksit Bharat – Guarantee for Rozgar and Ajeevika Mission (Gramin) (VB–G RAM G) Bill, 2025 — 16–18 December 2025\r\n\r\nThe Viksit Bharat – Guarantee for Rozgar and Ajeevika Mission (Gramin) Bill, 2025 was introduced in the Lok Sabha on 16 December 2025 and passed by Parliament on 18 December 2025. It seeks to replace the Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA), 2005 with a new statutory framework that guarantees enhanced rural employment, increased days of wage work, and strengthened planning under the Vision of Viksit Bharat 2047.\r\nSource: Press Information Bureau / PRS India\r\n🔗 https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2025/dec/doc20251218735801.pdf\r\n\r\n🔗 https://prsindia.org/files/bills_acts/bills_parliament/2025/Summary-Viksit_Bharat_GRamG_Bill_2025.pdf\r\n\r\n10. United States Attack on Venezuela & Abduction of Nicolás Maduro — 3 January 2026\r\n\r\nOn 3 January 2026, U.S. military forces launched a large-scale operation codename Operation Absolute Resolve against Venezuela, bombing targets in Caracas and capturing President Nicolás Maduro and his wife, Cilia Flores, before flying them to the United States. The attack drew intense global reaction, with Venezuelan officials condemning it as an abduction and violation of sovereignty.\r\nSource: Al Jazeera\r\n🔗 https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/4/how-the-us-attack-on-venezuela-abduction-of-maduro-unfolded\r\n\r\n11. India-EU-Trade-Deal - January 27, 2026\r\n\r\nOn 27 January 2026, India and the European Union finalized a long-awaited Free Trade Agreement (FTA) after nearly two decades of negotiations, announced at the India–EU Summit in New Delhi by PM Narendra Modi, European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen, and European Council President António Costa; the deal seeks to expand market access, reduce tariffs, and strengthen economic ties across a 2-billion-people market, while safeguarding sensitive sectors and supporting SMEs.\r\n\r\nSource: Press Information Bureau (PIB)\r\n🔗 https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2219065&reg=3&lang=2\r\n\r\n12. Union Budget of India 2026-27 — 1 February 2026\r\n\r\nThe Union Budget of India for the financial year 2026-27 was presented on 1 February 2026 by Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman. The budget outlines the government’s fiscal policy, expenditure priorities, and key reforms for the year, emphasizing infrastructure-led growth, manufacturing, and fiscal discipline.\r\n\r\nTotal expenditure was estimated at about ₹53.5 lakh crore, with non-debt receipts around ₹36.5 lakh crore and a fiscal deficit target of 4.3 % of GDP. Public capital expenditure was increased to around ₹12.2 lakh crore, showcasing a strong push for infrastructure investment.\r\n\r\nSource: Press Information Bureau (PIB) & Budget reports\r\n🔗 https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2221455&reg=3&lang=1",
