      "url": "https://github.com/madhurimarawat/UPSC-Notes-Resources/blob/3e9d46ce703ce18b9a161ca4b8819f789f31de46/Geography/Middle_East/Middle_Eastern_Countries.md",
      "text": "## Middle Eastern Countries\r\n\r\n### What is the **Middle East**?\r\n\r\nThe **Middle East** is a **geographical–political region**, not a continent.\r\nThe term was coined by **European (British) strategists in the early 20th century** to describe the area **east of Europe**, **west of South Asia**, and **south of Russia**.\r\n\r\n📌 **Most accepted meaning today:**\r\n\r\n> The region centered around **Western Asia** and **Egypt**, connecting **Asia, Africa, and Europe**, and holding major historical, cultural, religious, and energy (oil & gas) significance.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 🌍 Most Accepted List of **Middle East Countries**\r\n\r\nThis list is used by the **UN, World Bank, CIA World Factbook, and most academic sources**:\r\n\r\n#### **Western Asia (Core Middle East)**\r\n\r\n1. **Saudi Arabia**\r\n2. **United Arab Emirates (UAE)**\r\n3. **Qatar**\r\n4. **Kuwait**\r\n5. **Oman**\r\n6. **Yemen**\r\n7. **Iraq**\r\n8. **Iran**\r\n9. **Israel**\r\n10. **Jordan**\r\n11. **Lebanon**\r\n12. **Syria**\r\n13. **Bahrain**\r\n14. **Turkey** *(often included due to political and historical ties)*\r\n\r\n#### **North Africa (Commonly Included)**\r\n\r\n15. **Egypt** ✅ *(universally included because of the Sinai Peninsula in Asia)*\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 📊 Summary Table (Most Accepted Version)\r\n\r\n| Region       | Countries                                                                                          |\r\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\r\n| Western Asia | Saudi Arabia, UAE, Qatar, Kuwait, Oman, Yemen, Iraq, Iran, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Syria, Bahrain |\r\n| Transitional | Turkey                                                                                             |\r\n| North Africa | Egypt                                                                                              |\r\n\r\n**Total (most accepted): 15 countries**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### ❗ Important Notes\r\n\r\n* **Middle East ≠ Arab World**\r\n  (Iran, Israel, Turkey are **not Arab**)\r\n* **Middle East ≠ Islamic World**\r\n  (includes Jewish, Christian, and secular states)\r\n* **Afghanistan & Pakistan** ❌\r\n  → Usually classified as **South Asia**\r\n* **Sudan & Libya** ❌\r\n  → Usually classified as **North Africa**, not core Middle East\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 🧭 Why the Middle East is important\r\n\r\n* Birthplace of **Judaism, Christianity, and Islam**\r\n* Holds **~50% of world’s proven oil reserves**\r\n* Strategic trade routes (Suez Canal, Strait of Hormuz)\r\n* Major geopolitical influence\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 🏛️ Capitals of Middle East Countries (Most Accepted Version)\r\n\r\n| Country                    | Capital         |\r\n| -------------------------- | --------------- |\r\n| Saudi Arabia               | **Riyadh**      |\r\n| United Arab Emirates (UAE) | **Abu Dhabi**   |\r\n| Qatar                      | **Doha**        |\r\n| Kuwait                     | **Kuwait City** |\r\n| Oman                       | **Muscat**      |\r\n| Yemen                      | **Sana’a**      |\r\n| Iraq                       | **Baghdad**     |\r\n| Iran                       | **Tehran**      |\r\n| Israel                     | **Jerusalem**   |\r\n| Jordan                     | **Amman**       |\r\n| Lebanon                    | **Beirut**      |\r\n| Syria                      | **Damascus**    |\r\n| Bahrain                    | **Manama**      |\r\n| Turkey                     | **Ankara**      |\r\n| Egypt                      | **Cairo**       |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 📌 Important Points\r\n\r\n* **Damascus** is often called the **oldest continuously inhabited capital** in the world.\r\n* **Jerusalem** is religiously significant to **Judaism, Christianity, and Islam**.\r\n* **Ankara** (not Istanbul) is Turkey’s capital.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🌊 Gulf Countries\r\n\r\n### Middle East & Gulf Countries\r\n\r\n❌ **No**, *Middle East* ≠ *Gulf countries*\r\n✅ **Gulf countries are a PART of the Middle East**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## What are **Gulf countries**?\r\n\r\nThese are countries around the Persian (Arabian) Gulf, officially known as GCC countries.\r\nGCC stands for Gulf Cooperation Council - a regional political and economic alliance formed in 1981 to promote economic cooperation, security, and policy coordination among its member states.\r\n\r\n**6 Gulf (GCC) countries**\r\n\r\n* 🇸🇦 Saudi Arabia\r\n* 🇦🇪 United Arab Emirates\r\n* 🇶🇦 Qatar\r\n* 🇴🇲 Oman\r\n* 🇧🇭 Bahrain\r\n* 🇰🇼 Kuwait\r\n\r\n👉 These are the ones usually called **“Gulf countries”** in exams.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## What is the **Middle East** then?\r\n\r\nThe **Middle East** is a **larger region**, which includes:\r\n\r\n* **All Gulf countries**, PLUS\r\n* 🇮🇷 Iran\r\n* 🇮🇶 Iraq\r\n* 🇯🇴 Jordan\r\n* 🇮🇱 Israel\r\n* 🇱🇧 Lebanon\r\n* 🇸🇾 Syria\r\n* 🇾🇪 Yemen\r\n* 🇹🇷 Turkey (partly)\r\n* 🇪🇬 Egypt (often included)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Easy exam line to remember\r\n\r\n> **All Gulf countries are in the Middle East, but not all Middle East countries are Gulf countries.**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## One-liner memory trick 😄\r\n\r\n**“Gulf = water-side rich cousins, Middle East = whole family.”**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 📚 **Source**\r\n\r\n* 🌐 *Middle East – Definition & Country Classification*\r\n  🔗 [https://www.britannica.com/place/Middle-East](https://www.britannica.com/place/Middle-East)\r\n\r\n* 🏛️ *Middle East Countries & Regional Groupings* — **CIA World Factbook**\r\n  🔗 [https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/regions/middle-east/](https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/regions/middle-east/)\r\n\r\n* 🌍 *Geographical Regions & Political Definitions* — **United Nations Statistics Division (UNSD)**\r\n  🔗 [https://unstats.un.org/unsd/methodology/m49/](https://unstats.un.org/unsd/methodology/m49/)\r\n\r\n* 🛢️ *Oil Reserves & Strategic Importance of the Middle East* — **U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA)**\r\n  🔗 [https://www.eia.gov/international/overview/world](https://www.eia.gov/international/overview/world)\r\n\r\n* 🕌 *Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC): Formation, Members & Objectives* — **Official GCC Website**\r\n  🔗 [https://www.gcc-sg.org/en-us/Pages/default.aspx](https://www.gcc-sg.org/en-us/Pages/default.aspx)\r\n\r\n* 🗺️ *Middle East Map, Capitals & Regional Inclusion (Egypt, Turkey)* — **World Bank**\r\n  🔗 [https://www.worldbank.org/en/region/mena](https://www.worldbank.org/en/region/mena)",
